        <p>ACT, 1908. COUNTY OF LANCASTER. 111, °TICE IS HEREBY GIVEN, that FREDERIC 'PEY, Esq., the Commissioner appointed by the will hold an INQUIRY Eli)) As to the extent to which there is a demand for WALL HOLDINGS in or near the Township of 4-escot or would be a demand if suitable land were t allable ; and (2) as to the extent to which it is eepunably practicable, having regard to the provisions Act to satisfy any such demand. to.'"ue COMMISSIONER will attend at the Urban qatrict Council. Offices, Prescot, on TUESDAY, the heth day of September at the hour of seven p.m., when 11.. Will be prepared to see any persons who desire to or lease Holdings exceeding one acre and not teeeeding 50 acres which they are prepared themselves cultivate.</p>
