      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-09-11_WidnesExaminer_art0029" n="art0029">
        <head>September 11, 1909</head>
        <p>September 11, 1909</p>
        <p>BOWLING.</p>
        <p>ODDFELLOWS' MAIN.</p>
        <p>On Saturday afternoon a main under the auspices of of the 1.0.0. F. M.U., for the cup presented by Sir Gilbert Greenall and 32 prizes, was commenced on the green adjoning the King and Queen Hotel,Padgate-lane. There were 114 entrants, and some interesting games were witnessed. During the afternoon Mr. and Mrs. Robert Pierpoint visited the ground and Sir Gilbert Greenall telegraphed his inability to be present owing to his attendance at Knutsford Show. The main is to be completed on the 18th inst. The following are the details : _ _ _</p>
        <p>cV-.--B-u-tierworth w.o. W. Roughley, se J. Burrows A. Lawton A. Glover w.o A. Dutton — A. C. Hepburn S. Broadhurst — T. Howard w.o. J. M. Finch l3 I. Makin J. T. Mather _ H Wdd .. . 13 _</p>
