        <head>SHOOTING MATCH,</head>
        <p>SHOOTING MATCH,</p>
        <p>APPLETON -RIFLE CLUB v. DARESBUIa RIFLE CLUB. NI Last Saturday a team of ten men from the Dare Fe Rifle Club visited the range at Appleton for the Pugb• of shooting a return match with the Appleton fog The weather was far from favourable, rain commein,coo- to fall soon after the beginning of the match, ana "tbe tinning until the close. In spite of this, however, to, interest on both sides was very keen and a good rOB,O resulted. The conditions were as follows :—Each Le 0 to consist of ten men, the best scores on each siuibis count. Miniature rifles, any sights bar telescopic, jog year's Standard N.R.A. Targets, and the disapPetlerthe figure. Ten shots at the 3in. bull, and ten shots a. 'bet disappearing figure. Distance, IC3 yards. gig tbe possible score, 80 per man oran aggregate of 610 'lgo team. The match resulted in a victory for the APP Club who made a score of 485 against 411 by the .1-'3‘ 4; bury Club, the former thus winning by a majority 0' points. The following scores were made : APPLETON RIFLE CLUB. - Disappearing , 3in. ball. figure. Tots,. H. Potts, inn J. Gardiner 43 21 ' 67 H. Potts, sen. 4l 21 62 C. W. Bowyer 3B 21 59 . C. P. Day 3l 27 58 E. Pollard 4O 18 58 A. Shepherd A. B. Mellor - ...--- • 485 , _ _</p>
        <p>Other scares :-- - A. E. Longshaiv 31 21 52 .1. Sankey 3l 12 46 ' DARESEURY RIFLE CLUB. Rev. .1. S. Barnes 41 21 62 .1. Grosvenor T. Speed C. Ryder G. Tickle 42 15 57 C. Sbepherd-Cross 32 21 53 T. B. Cotterhill D. Dono</p>
