        <head>BOY SCOUTS AT CRYSTAL PALACE.</head>
        <p>BOY SCOUTS AT CRYSTAL PALACE.</p>
        <p>Eleven thousand boy scouts tcok patt in the first annual rally at the Crystal Palace, kid from early morning until late at night the great glass house and grounds at Sydenbarn Were given over to little lids in short knickers, Wild West shirts, and B.P. hats. The boys, 'ho were inspected by General Baden-Powell, came from all parts of England, Scotland, and Wales, and the march past, which, owing to the rain, took placein. the Palace, was very lyell done ind-ed. A feature of the rally was the reading of a message from the King.</p>
