      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-09-11_WidnesExaminer_art0085" n="art0085">
        <head>DR. COOK LANDS AT COPENHAGEN.</head>
        <p>DR. COOK LANDS AT COPENHAGEN.</p>
        <p>Dr. Cook, who claims to have been the first man to reach the North Po'e, landed at cPenhagen on Saturday. The worn at that time was divided into Cookites and anti- `-ookites, but there was certainly no doubting the enthusiasm of his welcome to the Danish fp. His reception was tumultuous. The Crown Prince of Denmark went on board the au Egede to meet Dr. Cook, and King Frederick had an account of his adventures from the , explorer's lips. Dr. Cook says that those who are sceptical as to his claim will be : convinced without a shadow of doubt." He does not claim to have reached the "exact 'Pot" of the Pole but the magic circle where a gun shot would have passed over the actual „P2ita• Here he left a sealed metal tube containing a record of his achievement. Out rilOtograph shows Dr. Cook landing at Copenhagen.</p>
