        <p>HE MEDICAL INSTITUTE OF E LEC- TRICITY.—DO YOU SUFFER from Rheu- matism, Sciatica, Insomnia, Nervous Prostration, Loss of Memory, i Paralysis, Deafness, Neuralgia, Stammer- ing, Pains n the Head and Back, Depression of Spirits, Dimness of Sight, Dread of Future Events, Nervous Timidity? ALL NERVOUS and MENTAL DIS- ORDERS CURED by Dr. Fisher, U.S.A., Brain and Nerve Specialist, 263, Kensington, LIVERPOOL.. 10 to 3 and sto 8 p.m. Modern Scientific Massage and Electro.Vibro Medical Massage. Electricity. Con- sultations free. MUNICIPAL BYE-ELECTION.—TO THE ELECTORS OF HOWLEY WARD. LADIES AND GMsTTLEMENt Owing to the lamented death of my friend, the late Mr. Councillor W. B. Roberts, a vacancy has occurred in the representation of your Ward. At the unanimous request of the Conservative Ward Committee and at the wish of many Electors of all shades of politics" hgve consented to come forward as a Candidate. All my interests are identified with the town, and I am sincerely anxious to do whatever I can to promote its welfare and to further its prosperity. There are many vital questions awaiting solution. I may specially mention the Widening of Warrington Bridge, the Provision of Better Access from the Howley Ward to the Victoria Park, the Completion of the Circus at Market Gate and the Widening of our Main Streets. I am in favour of a policy of steady Municipal Pro- gress, and believe that it was never more important than now to take a broad and comprehensive view of our Municipal Responsibilities. Every public-spirited citizen should be prepared to do his utmost to assist in the great task of Improving the Town and bringing it into line with all the Most Progressive Boroughs in the Kingdom. Whilst lam a Conservative in politics, I shall retain my right to act as I think beat on all Municipal- Questionsiernd be guided-solely-by strictatimt f duty to the town I honestly desire to serve. I am, Ladies and Gentlemen, Your obedient servant, CHARLES DUTTON PARKINSON. Bevrsey Chambers, Warrington. 3rd September, 1909.</p>
